input/.git/HEAD makes input a git repository: outln applies .gitignore files only inside one.
== args
input/src
input/src/generated.md
== file input/.git/HEAD
ref: refs/heads/main
== file input/.gitignore
generated.md
== file input/src/a.md
---
description: A summary.
---
# a
== file input/src/generated.md
---
description: Explicitly named, so listed despite .gitignore.
---
# generated
== stdout
glob view: input/src input/src/generated.md
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/src/a.md: description: "A summary."
input/src/generated.md: description: "Explicitly named, so listed despite .gitignore."
